{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "Evidence: We have only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → acc 0.485, F1 0.464), so virtually all design dimensions—modality, encoder choice, profile setting, aggregation, and fusion—are unexplored. The most critical uncertainty right now is whether the image modality carries any useful signal for this task at all; without knowing that, we cannot rationally invest in multimodal fusion experiments. Question: config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) directly tests whether image features alone are informative, using the same profile setting and the same level of architectural simplicity as config_001, so the only variable that changes is the modality. Why this is the best next experiment: It provides a clean, single-variable comparison (RNA vs. image) that calibrates our expectations for every downstream multimodal experiment. If image-only is strong, multimodal fusion becomes a high-value direction; if it is weak, we can focus budget on RNA-side improvements (encoder, profile, aggregation) rather than spending experiments on fusion strategies that may add little. This maximizes information gain per experiment under the limited budget."
}

